redient in 6 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Red onions (also known as purple or blue onions in some mainland European countries) are cultivars of the onion (Allium cepa), and have purplish-red skin and white flesh tinged with red. They are most commonly used in cooking, but the skin has also been used as a dye."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-red-onion"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_onion"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Gudeg","dish/gudeg"],["Lemper","dish/lemper"],["Saksang","dish/saksang"],["Semur (Indonesian stew)","dish/semur-indonesian-stew"]]],["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Shaking beef","dish/shaking-beef"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Onions and shallots, dry (excluding dehydrated)","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":108951896,"top":[["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",27778742],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",24236603],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",3442287],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",3332490],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",2472400],["Bangladesh","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",2440794],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",2127541],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",2119506],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",1974670],["Niger","cuisine/cuisine-of-niger",1755354],["Algeria","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",1750906],["Netherlands","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",1704528],["Russia","cuisine/russian-cuisine",1648614],["Sudan","cuisine/sudanese-cuisine",1627951],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",1623854]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Andaliman","ingredient/andaliman"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Bay leaf","ingredient/bay-leaf